1. **A circuit comprising:**

   a substrate;

   an array of programmable memory elements disposed on the substrate, each programmable memory element being associated with a respective programmable region of the substrate, wherein a logic state of each programmable memory element is set by externally applying a programming material to, or omitting the programming material from, the respective programmable region;

   a first plurality of control lines coupled to the array of programmable memory elements and configured to provide access to selected programmable memory elements of the array for reading the logic states thereof; and

   a plurality of additional circuit elements disposed on the substrate and coupled to a second plurality of control lines, the second plurality of control lines being separate from the first plurality of control lines and configured to control operation of the additional circuit elements.

1. **A programmable integrated circuit structure**, comprising:  
   a substrate;  
   a plurality of programmable memory elements fabricated on the substrate, each programmable memory element being configurable between at least a first stored state and a second stored state;  
   a first set of control lines coupled to the plurality of programmable memory elements and configured to address selected ones of the plurality of programmable memory elements;  
   a second set of control lines coupled to the plurality of programmable memory elements, wherein each programmable memory element is addressable by application of signals to at least one line of the first set of control lines and at least one line of the second set of control lines;  
   one or more post-fabrication deposited material regions disposed over selected regions of the substrate, the one or more post-fabrication deposited material regions defining programmed states of selected ones of the plurality of programmable memory elements; and  
   a plurality of additional addressable circuit elements fabricated on the substrate, the additional addressable circuit elements being coupled to the second set of control lines.

2. **The programmable integrated circuit structure of claim 1**, wherein the one or more post-fabrication deposited material regions comprise conductive material deposited after completion of fabrication of the plurality of programmable memory elements.

3. **The programmable integrated circuit structure of claim 1**, wherein the one or more post-fabrication deposited material regions comprise dielectric, resistive, semiconductive, or conductive material selected to alter an electrical characteristic of the selected programmable memory elements.

4. **The programmable integrated circuit structure of claim 1**, wherein the programmed states are determined by whether a post-fabrication deposited material region is present or absent over a corresponding programmable memory element.

5. **The programmable integrated circuit structure of claim 1**, wherein the first set of control lines comprises word lines and the second set of control lines comprises bit lines.

6. **The programmable integrated circuit structure of claim 1**, wherein the additional addressable circuit elements comprise logic elements, switching elements, sensor elements, driver elements, or memory elements.

7. **The programmable integrated circuit structure of claim 1**, wherein the plurality of programmable memory elements and the plurality of additional addressable circuit elements share at least one common line of the second set of control lines.

8. **A method of programming an integrated circuit structure**, comprising:  
   fabricating, on a substrate, a plurality of programmable memory elements;  
   coupling the plurality of programmable memory elements to at least a first set of control lines and a second set of control lines such that individual programmable memory elements are addressable using signals applied to the first and second sets of control lines;  
   fabricating additional addressable circuit elements on the substrate, the additional addressable circuit elements being coupled to the second set of control lines; and  
   after fabrication of the programmable memory elements, depositing material over selected regions of the substrate to program selected ones of the programmable memory elements.

9. **The method of claim 8**, wherein depositing material over selected regions comprises selectively depositing material over regions corresponding to memory elements to be programmed to a predetermined logical state.

10. **The method of claim 8**, wherein depositing material over selected regions is performed using mask-based deposition, direct-write deposition, printing, inkjet deposition, laser-assisted deposition, or additive material placement.

11. **The method of claim 8**, wherein depositing material over selected regions changes a resistance, capacitance, conductivity, threshold voltage, optical property, magnetic property, or coupling characteristic of the selected programmable memory elements.

12. **A post-fabrication programmable memory array**, comprising:  
   an array of memory cells disposed on a substrate;  
   a plurality of first address lines extending in a first direction and coupled to the memory cells;  
   a plurality of second address lines extending in a second direction and coupled to the memory cells, each memory cell being selectable by a corresponding first address line and a corresponding second address line;  
   deposited programming material located over selected memory cells after formation of the array, the deposited programming material encoding stored data in the array; and  
   a plurality of non-memory addressable circuit elements coupled to at least one of the plurality of second address lines.

1. An integrated circuit apparatus comprising:

a semiconductor substrate;

a plurality of programmable memory cells disposed on the semiconductor substrate, each programmable memory cell having a programmable state determined by whether a material is applied to cover a selected region associated with the programmable memory cell;

a first plurality of control lines extending in a first direction and coupled to the plurality of programmable memory cells;

a second plurality of control lines extending in a second direction and coupled to the plurality of programmable memory cells, the first plurality of control lines and the second plurality of control lines being configured to address selected ones of the plurality of programmable memory cells by row and column selection; and

a plurality of non-memory circuit elements disposed on the semiconductor substrate, each non-memory circuit element being connected between a respective one of the first plurality of control lines and a respective one of a third plurality of control lines,

wherein the plurality of programmable memory cells and the plurality of non-memory circuit elements are integrated on the semiconductor substrate, and wherein the material applied to cover selected regions defines programmed states of corresponding ones of the programmable memory cells.
